{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Of the travail.</b> The meaning: the reward that he will receive for having endured." "<b>He shall see.</b> His desire, or he shall see good, until he is sated, because by his knowledge he will justify many — and they are the nations, whom Israel will teach to do the Torah." "And the meaning of <b>and their iniquities he shall bear</b>: that Israel will share in the suffering of the nations on account of their many iniquities, not as they did to Israel. Or the meaning: that he will pray to HaShem on behalf of the nations, in the sense of and if the family of Egypt does not go up (Zechariah 14:18). And this is the correct one in my eyes, for the verse that follows it is a witness."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:22.532938150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}